@Haroenv Hi, thanks I tried that way but there is an unexpected problem. When I search by dates.start and dates.end Algolia doesn't search it as a pair so the result are wrong. For example:

![Captura de pantalla 2023-06-14 a las 17 23 44](https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch/assets/13077343/4cbb7bb7-d110-4037-aa09-fa6feeb4a301)

In the example, you can see that the results are incorrect because Algolia has returned an item that has a start date of 2023-06-06 and an end date of 2023-09-01, but it has not searched for them as if they were a pair.
